<title>JAPAN: Strict criteria must be applied for EMU-EC&quot;s Keck.</title>
<headline>Strict criteria must be applied for EMU-EC&quot;s Keck.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strict criteria must be applied for admission to the European economic and monetary union (EMU), Joern Keck, ambassador and head of delegation of the European Commission in Japan, said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no room for fudging figures or cooking the books,&quot; he told a seminar on EMU in Tokyo.</p>
<p>He said the European Commission would not recommend any countries that used &quot;one-off tricks&quot; if it was obvious that criteria would not be kept afterwards.</p>
<p>He also said there was no reason to expect the euro &quot;to be too strong or too weak for any exchange rate&quot;.</p>
</text>
